Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 04:19:16 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] windows: cpu-template-helper's fingerprint names the host
 from the registry

A fingerprint names the host's microcode revision and its BIOS's version and
release, which Linux reads from /proc/cpuinfo and the DMI files in sysfs.
Windows keeps the same facts in the registry: the revision the processor
reported at boot (CentralProcessor\0, "Update Revision": Intel's in the
high half, AMD's the whole value) and the SMBIOS BIOS values
(System\BIOS). They are read there, in Linux's format (0xa60120c, FB5,
5.35 on the WHP PC); a sysfs path the helper does not map is not found, as
on Linux.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
